%% CURRENT — training-worker lifecycle as implemented in the worker code (tested against local fakes; run on AWS per the owner).
%% Design source: the owner's "Terraform & project structure" design notes (training-instance shutdown control flow),
%% cross-checked against the worker's AWS adapters (receive / claim / protection / visibility / delete order).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Q as SQS training queue
    participant W as Training worker (GPU instance)
    participant S3 as S3 (datasets · adapters)
    participant ASG as Auto Scaling group
    participant API as FastAPI backend

    W->>Q: ReceiveMessage (long poll, one job)
    W->>S3: Claim the job (conditional write)
    W->>ASG: SetInstanceProtection(true)
    loop While training (QLoRA)
        W->>Q: ChangeMessageVisibility (lease heartbeat, stop work if the lease is lost)
        W->>S3: Write checkpoint
    end
    W->>W: Reload and evaluate the adapter
    W->>S3: Publish adapter files + manifest (SHA-256), then the READY marker
    W->>API: Result callback (token-authenticated)
    API-->>W: 200 OK (state persisted)
    W->>Q: DeleteMessage (only after the backend confirms)
    W->>ASG: SetInstanceProtection(false)
    Note over ASG: Queue empty and no protected instances, so the ASG scales in to zero
    Note over W,Q: On failure the message is not deleted: it becomes visible again (retry) or moves to the DLQ
